KNOWNBUG
word_constant_out_of_range1.smv

outside of its width
^EXIT=2$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
convert_word_constant (smv_typecheck.cpp) never checks that the decimal
value of a sized word constant fits into its declared width; it just
calls from_integer, which silently wraps the value modulo 2^width. Here
0ud4_20 (a 4-bit unsigned constant) silently becomes 4 (20 mod 16)
instead of being rejected, so the model is built from a value the user
never wrote and LTLSPEC G(a = 0ud4_4) is wrongly reported PROVED. NuSMV
rejects the same input with a parse error ("value ... is outside of its
width").
